    "turn_text": "age of 18, you know, by someone else. And it also would be extended far beyond that group, actually, to individuals who have, or even would be eligible for TPS, which is temporary protective status, and deferred enforced departure status, which is always intended as kind of a temporary opportunity for persons coming from other nations or torn nations, for instance, or nations dealing with a natural catastrophe. It was never intended to provide permanent status or citizenship. So essentially what it does is gives these individuals the opportunity to have immediate permanent status and an immediate special pathway to citizenship allows them to kind of jump ahead of all the folks that have been doing it right and have been waiting for their opportunities to come into America for many,",
